Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

The aggregation, schema, and pipeline code in this repository are released
under CC BY 4.0.

The underlying source datasets have varying license terms (see per-dataset
notes below). The "all CC BY" shorthand does not apply to all sources.

Attribution requirements:

You must cite the underlying source publications when using this data.

--- CC BY 4.0 sources ---

  - Sharma, P., Gero, S., Payne, R., Gruber, D. F., Rus, D., Torralba, A.,
    & Andreas, J. (2024). Contextual and combinatorial structure in sperm
    whale vocalisations. Nature Communications, 15(1), 3617.
    doi:10.1038/s41467-024-47221-8
    License: CC BY 4.0 (Nature Communications open access)

  - Sharma, P., et al. (2025). Sperm whale live birth coda recordings.
    Scientific Reports. doi:10.1038/s41598-025-27438-3
    License: CC BY 4.0 (Scientific Reports open access)

  - Bermant, P. C., Bronstein, M. M., Wood, R. J., Gero, S., & Gruber, D. F.
    (2019). Deep machine learning techniques for the detection and
    classification of sperm whale bioacoustics. Scientific Reports, 9, 12588.
    doi:10.1038/s41598-019-48909-4
    Data files: 41598_2019_48909_MOESM2_ESM.xlsx, ETP.xlsx (MOESM3)
    License: CC BY 4.0 (Scientific Reports open access)

--- CC0 sources (Dryad) ---

  - Gero, S., Bottcher, A., Whitehead, H., & Madsen, P. T. (2016). Socially
    segregated, sympatric sperm whale clans in the Atlantic Ocean. Royal
    Society Open Science, 3(6), 160061.
    Data: Dryad doi:10.5061/dryad.53g73
    License: CC0 (Dryad default)

  - Gero, S., Whitehead, H., & Rendell, L. (2016). Individual, unit and vocal
    clan level identity cues in sperm whale codas. Royal Society Open
    Science, 3(1), 150372.
    Data: Dryad doi:10.5061/dryad.ck4h0
    License: CC0 (Dryad default)
    Note: raw file present in data/raw/ but not used by the current pipeline.

--- No explicit license declared (OSF deposits) ---

  - Hersh, T. A., Gero, S., Rendell, L., & Whitehead, H. (2022). Evidence
    from sperm whale clans of symbolic marking in non-human cultures.
    Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 119(37), e2201692119.
    doi:10.1073/pnas.2201692119
    Data: OSF https://osf.io/ae6pd/
    License: The OSF deposit carries no declared license. The PNAS paper is
    open access (CC BY 4.0). Users who redistribute this data should
    verify current terms on the OSF deposit page.

  - Beguš, G., et al. (2026). The phonology of sperm whale coda vowels.
    Data: OSF https://osf.io/9t6qu/
    License: The OSF deposit carries no declared license. Users who
    redistribute this data should verify current terms on the OSF deposit
    page and cite the associated publication.

--- CC BY-NC-ND (non-commercial, no derivatives) ---

  - Hersh, T. A., Gero, S., Rendell, L., & Whitehead, H. (2021). Using
    identity calls to detect structure in acoustic datasets. Methods in
    Ecology and Evolution, 12(7). doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13644
    Data: OSF https://osf.io/5fter/ (IDcallR_SpermWhaleCodas.csv)
    License: CC BY-NC-ND (paper); OSF deposit shows "No License" for the
    data file itself. Under the most conservative reading, CC BY-NC-ND
    applies — non-commercial use only, no derivatives.
    Note: this file is not included in the repo; download it from OSF and
    place it at data/raw/IDcallR_SpermWhaleCodas.csv before running the
    pipeline. Contact taylor.a.hersh@gmail.com with redistribution questions.

The CC BY 4.0 license text (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
applies to the aggregation, schema, and pipeline code in this repository.
Each source dataset retains its own upstream license as noted above.
